{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Recurrent Neural Networks\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Modeling Sequential Data with Memory\"\n",
        "author: \"Miguel Fonseca\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  revealjs:\n",
        "    toc: true\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Why Do We Need RNNs?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Feedforward Networks Assume Independence\n",
        "\n",
        "For MLPs:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "x_i \\perp x_j\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "But many datasets are sequential:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Text\n",
        "- Speech\n",
        "- Financial time-series\n",
        "- Biological sequences\n",
        "- Sensor signals\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Sequential Dependency\n",
        "\n",
        "Language modeling:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(w_t | w_{t-1}, w_{t-2}, ..., w_1)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The past matters.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Applications\n",
        "\n",
        "- Language modeling\n",
        "- Machine translation\n",
        "- Speech recognition\n",
        "- Time-series forecasting\n",
        "- Genomics\n",
        "- Video processing\n",
        "\n",
        "# The Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Core Recurrence\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h_t = \\sigma(W_h h_{t-1} + W_x x_t + b)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "y_t = W_y h_t\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Same weights reused across time.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Unrolled Through Time\n",
        "\n",
        "![Unrolled RNN](/images/rnn_unrolled.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## TensorFlow: Simple RNN"
      ],
      "id": "5ec8570c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from tensorflow import keras\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
        "\n",
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    layers.SimpleRNN(64, return_sequences=True),\n",
        "    layers.SimpleRNN(32),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(1)\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "model.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"mse\")\n",
        "model.summary()"
      ],
      "id": "684dcc03",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Backpropagation Through Time (BPTT)\n",
        "\n",
        "Training objective:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial W} =\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial h_t}\\frac{\\partial h_t}{\\partial W}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "But:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\partial h_t}{\\partial h_{t-k}}=\\prod_{i=t-k+1}^{t}\\frac{\\partial h_i}{\\partial h_{i-1}}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Repeated matrix multiplication → instability.\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## The Vanishing Gradient Problem\n",
        "\n",
        "Simplified Recurrence\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h_t = \\sigma(W_h h_{t-1})\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Derivative:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\partial h_t}{\\partial h_{t-1}}\n",
        "=\n",
        "W_h \\cdot \\text{diag}(1 - \\sigma^2(z))\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Since:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "|1 - \\sigma^2(z)| \\le 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Repeated products:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\prod_{i=1}^{k} W_h \\lambda_i\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "If:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\rho(W_h) < 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ">Gradient vanishes.\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "If:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\rho(W_h) > 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ">Exploding gradient.\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "# Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Key Idea\n",
        "\n",
        "![LSTM Cell](/images/lstm_architecture.png)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.callout-note}\n",
        "Allow constant error flow through a memory cell.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## LSTM Equations\n",
        "\n",
        "**Forget gate:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "f_t = \\sigma(W_f [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Input gate:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "i_t = \\sigma(W_i [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Cell update:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "c_t = f_t \\odot c_{t-1} + i_t \\odot \\tilde{c}_t\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Output:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h_t = o_t \\odot \\tanh(c_t)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why LSTM Works\n",
        "\n",
        "If:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "f_t \\approx 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\frac{\\partial c_t}{\\partial c_{t-1}} \\approx 1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ">Gradient preserved.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tensorflow: LSTM"
      ],
      "id": "360251f2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    layers.LSTM(64, return_sequences=True),\n",
        "    layers.LSTM(32),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(1)\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "model.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"mse\")"
      ],
      "id": "24692e50",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU)\n",
        "\n",
        "## GRU Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        ">Simpler alternative to LSTM.\n",
        "\n",
        "![GRU Cell](/images/gru_architecture.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "## GRU Equations\n",
        "\n",
        "**Update gate:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "z_t = \\sigma(W_z [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Reset gate:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "r_t = \\sigma(W_r [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Final Update:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h_t = (1 - z_t) \\odot h_{t-1} + z_t \\odot \\widetilde{h}_t\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tensorflow: GRU"
      ],
      "id": "b0e84c64"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    layers.GRU(64, return_sequences=True),\n",
        "    layers.GRU(32),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(1)\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "id": "2a2e73ed",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Regularization in RNNs\n",
        "\n",
        "## Recurrent Dropout\n",
        "\n",
        "Standard dropout disrupts temporal memory.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Recurrent dropout:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Applied on recurrent connections\n",
        "- Same mask across timesteps\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## TensorFlow: Recurrent Dropout"
      ],
      "id": "78d92684"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    layers.LSTM(\n",
        "        64,\n",
        "        return_sequences=True,\n",
        "        dropout=0.2,\n",
        "        recurrent_dropout=0.2\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    layers.LSTM(32),\n",
        "    layers.Dense(1)\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "id": "995337ca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Gradient Clipping\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\nabla_\\theta L \\leftarrow \\frac{\\nabla_\\theta L}{\\max(1, \\frac{||\\nabla_\\theta L||}{\\text{clipnorm}})}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Prevent exploding gradients:"
      ],
      "id": "eee12ed5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "optimizer = tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.001,\n",
        "    clipnorm=1.0\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "9722c82d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Extensions\n",
        "\n",
        "## Deep RNNs\n",
        "\n",
        "Stack multiple RNN layers for hierarchical representations:\n",
        "\n",
        "![Deep RNN](/images/deep_rnn.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Bidirectional RNNs\n",
        "\n",
        "Process sequences in both directions:\n",
        "\n",
        "![Bidirectional RNN](/images/bidirectional_rnn.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Final Notes\n",
        "\n",
        "## Model Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Long Dependencies | Complexity | Speed  |\n",
        "| ----- | ----------------- | ---------- | ------ |\n",
        "| RNN   | Poor              | Low        | Fast   |\n",
        "| LSTM  | Excellent         | High       | Slower |\n",
        "| GRU   | Very Good         | Medium     | Faster |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Limitations of RNNs\n",
        "\n",
        "- Sequential computation\n",
        "- Hard to parallelize\n",
        "- Long sequences still challenging\n",
        "- Transformers dominate NLP"
      ],
      "id": "c4938b73"
    }
  ],
